===Garuda Shield 2011===
[[File:Garuda Shield 2011.jpg|thumb|Brig. Gen. Michele G. Compton, the commanding general of the 9th Mission Support Command, and Brig. Gen. Mulyono, the training director for the Indonesian Army Training and Doctrine Command giving opening speech during Garuda Shield 2011.]]
Garuda Shield 2011 was returned to an annual bilateral exercise that focus on three main components: Command Post Exercise, Field Training Exercise, and humanitarian civic action project. The Opening ceremony of Garuda Shield 2011 was carried out on 10 June 2011, at the Engineer Training Center of Army Education and Training Command, Pusdikzi, [[Bogor]], [[West Java]].<ref name=":13" /><ref>{{Cite web  |last=Douglas |first=Christina |date=10 June 2011 |title=US, Indonesia partner for Exercise Garuda Shield 2011 |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/image/414322/us-indonesia-partner-exercise-garuda-shield-2011 |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref>

During the opening ceremony, Brig. Gen. [[Michele G. Compton]], the commanding general of the 9th MSC, welcomed the troops and described the importance of the regionally significant training event.<ref name="AutoPD-8">{{Cite web |last=Douglas |first=Christina |date=13 June 2011 |title=US, Indonesia partner for Exercise Garuda Shield 2011 |url=https://www.army.mil/article/59478/us_indonesia_partner_for_exercise_garuda_shield_2011 |access-date=29 July 2022 |website=www.army.mil |language=en}}{{source-attribution}}</ref>

“Garuda Shield is an opportunity for the Indonesian Army and the United States Army to come together in a learning environment to share experiences and lessons learned with each other. Of equal importance during this exercise, is the opportunity to form and maintain close friendships and also to gain an enduring appreciation of each other’s customs,” said Compton.<REF name="AutoPD-8"/>

The 12-day training, which was attended by 631 [[Indonesian Army|TNI AD]] personnel and 141 personnel from [[United States Army Pacific|USARPAC]], aims to improve interoperability among trainees and prepare capacity building facilities for UN troop-sending countries. Director of Training of the [[Indonesian Army Doctrine, Education and Training Development Command|Indonesian Army Doctrine, Education and Training Development Command (Kodiklat TNI-AD)]] [[Brigadier general|Brig. Gen.]] [[Mulyono]] said the joint military exercise between the two countries was conducted to place the cooperation in the United Nations peace-keeping operation on a solid footing. He said the regular annual exercise this year in Bogor involved Indonesian Ground Force and United States Army Pacific, an [[Army Service Component Command]] of the United States Army and is the army component unit of the United States Pacific Command.

"Such an exercise is the fifth of its kind because Indonesia is frequently involved in UN peace-keeping missions," Mulyono said.

He added that the "Garuda Shield" exercise in general was intended to step up the relations between the two countries` ground forces.

"The joint exercise with the US is of great advantage in the face of peace-keeping operation dynamics, and the way how to integrate the system of training in Indonesia and the United States," Mulyono said. Garuda Shield 2011 concluded on 22 June 2011.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Syafputri |first=Ella |date=10 June 2011 |title=RI, US conduct joint military exercise in Bogor |url=https://en.antaranews.com/news/72556/ri-us-conduct-joint-military-exercise-in-bogor |access-date=29 July 2022 |website=Antara News}}</ref>

===Garuda Shield 2012===
The opening ceremony of Garuda Shield 2012 between the Indonesian Army (TNI AD) and the United States Army Pacific (USARPAC) was held at the [[Kostrad 2nd Infantry Division]] Headquarters in [[Singosari]], [[Malang Regency]], East Java, Monday, 11 June 2012, led by Lt. Gen. [[M. Munir]], Commander of Kostrad accompanied by Brig. Gen. [[Gary M. Hara]], Commander of [[Hawaii Army National Guard]].<ref name=":14">{{Cite web |date=11 June 2012 |title=TNI AD dan Tentara AS Latihan Perang Bareng |url=https://www.tempo.co/arsip/tni-ad-dan-tentara-as-latihan-perang-bareng-1677583 |access-date= |website=Tempo |language=id}}</ref>

The joint exercise, said Lieutenant General TNI M Munir, involved 456 Indonesian Army personnel and 104 USARPAC personnel. The activities that will be carried out include the command post exercise which will be held at the Rindam Brawijaya PLDC and the field training exercise which will be held in the training area in Rindam V Brawijaya Sidodadi [[Lawang, Malang|Lawang]], [[Malang]], and ''Karya Bhakti'' (ENCAP) which will be held in Purwosari, [[Pasuruan Regency|Pasuruan]].<ref name=":15">{{Cite web |last=Ainun |first=Yatimul |date=11 June 2012 |title=TNI AD Latihan Bersama Militer AS |url=https://nasional.kompas.com/read/2012/06/11/11085194/~Nasional |access-date=31 July 2022 |website=Kompas |language=id}}</ref>

U.S. Army Reserve Soldiers with the 871st Engineer Company, 411th Engineer Battalion, headquartered in Hilo, Hawaii, and their counterparts with the Tentara National Indonesia Angkatan Darat, or TNI-AD, are accomplishing both tasks as they work side by side to build a community center in Malang, Indonesia, as part of Garuda Shield 2012.<ref name="AutoPD-10">{{Cite web |first=Andrew A. |last=Reagan |date=21 June 2012 |title=Engineers build community center, partnership with Indonesian forces during Garuda Shield 2012 |url=https://www.army.mil/article/82145/engineers_build_community_center_partnership_with_indonesian_forces_during_garuda_shield_2012 |access-date= |website=www.army.mil |language=en}}{{source-attribution}}</ref>

In its sixth year, Garuda Shield is a combined exercise between the TNI-AD and U.S. Army that improves peacekeeping, stability operations and increases the disaster relief capabilities of both armies. A major part of the exercise is the community center construction project, as well as a sister project to renovate a family welfare center in the same part of Malang.<REF name="AutoPD-10"/>

Garuda Shield 2012 concluded on 22 June 2012.<ref name=":14" /><ref name=":15" />

===Garuda Shield 2013===
On 10 June 2013, the Indonesian Army and United States Army held the opening ceremony of Garuda Shield 2013 at the [[Kostrad 1st Infantry Division]] Headquarters in [[Depok]], West Java, Indonesia. The Honorable Scot Marciel, U.S. Ambassador to the Republic of Indonesia, and exercise co-directors Maj. Gen. [[Gary M. Hara]], Deputy Commanding General for the Army National Guard, U.S. Army Pacific (USARPAC) and Maj. Gen. [[Daniel Ambat]], Kostrad 1st Division Commander, spoke at the ceremony.<ref name="Auto2A-7">{{Cite web |first=Corine |last=Lombardo |date=11 June 2013 |title=Joint US Army/Indonesia Exercise 'Garuda Shield' Begins |url=https://www.army.mil/article/105265/joint_us_armyindonesia_exercise_garuda_shield_begins |access-date= |website=www.army.mil |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Exercise Garuda Shield |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/video/294493/exercise-garuda-shield |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=DVIDS |language=en}}{{source-attribution}}</ref>

Garuda Shield 2013 lasted for 12 days, from 10 to 21 June 2013. Deputy Commanding General of the U.S. Army National Guard in the Pacific (USARPAC), Gary M Hara, said 312 U.S. Army personnel participated in the exercise. Meanwhile, 300 personnel from Indonesia. The exercise includes planning and executing a combined brigade-level command post exercise based on a United Nations (U.N.) scenario and a field-training exercise based on a rescue operation scenario. The exercise involved troops from U.S. Army Pacific (USARPAC); the Indonesian Army National Army (TNI-AD), Kostrad 1st Division; 1st Battalion, 504th Parachute Infantry Regiment, 82nd Airborne Division; and the Indonesian Army, 17th Airborne Brigade.<ref name="Auto2A-7"/><ref name=":4">{{Cite web |last=Armandhanu |first=Denny |date=10 June 2013 |title=Tentara AS-Indonesia Latihan Perang Bersama |url=https://www.viva.co.id/berita/dunia/419499-tentara-as-indonesia-latihan-perang-bersama |access-date= |website=www.viva.co.id |language=id}}</ref>

Along with a series of parachute jumps, about 500 paratroopers of both nations conducted infantry training and operations during the exercise. The exercise focused on developing the respective militaries' ability to contribute to U.N. peace support operations, and on strengthening the nations' growing military relationships.<ref name="Auto2A-7"/><ref name=":4" />

===Garuda Shield 2014===
[[File:Garuda Shield 2014 opening ceremony 140901-A-ZO853-051.jpg|thumb|The Opening Ceremony of Garuda Shield 2014, 1 September 2014.]]
[[File:Garuda Shield (15030956879).jpg|thumb|U.S Army AH-64E Apache Guardian and Indonesian Army Mi-35 Attack Helicopter during Garuda Shield 2014, 9 September 2014.]]
[[File:Garuda Shield 2014 night illumination 140919-A-JK968-920.jpg|thumb|U.S and Indonesian Army carried out mortar exercise during Garuda Shield 2014, 19 September 2014.]]

The opening ceremony of the 2014 Garuda Shield training exercise was held on 1 September 2014 at Dodiklatpur Rindam V/BRW Asembagus, [[Situbondo Regency|Situbondo]], East Java, led by Indonesian Army Maj. Gen. [[Bambang Hariyanto,]] commander, [[Kostrad 2nd Infantry Division|2nd Infantry Division]], Kostrad and Lt. Gen. [[Stephen Lanza]], commander, [[I Corps (United States)|U.S. Army, I Corps]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Erickson |first=Brian |date=3 September 2014 |title=Indonesian, US exercise Garuda Shield begins in East Java |url=https://www.army.mil/article/132957/indonesian_us_exercise_garuda_shield_begins_in_east_java |access-date= |website=www.army.mil |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=2 September 2014 |title=TNI AD Dan US Army Laksanakan Latihan Bersama Garuda Shield-8/2014 |url=https://tniad.mil.id/tni-ad-dan-us-army-laksanakan-latihan-bersama-garuda-shield-82014/ |access-date= |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref>

This joint exercise was held for 1 month starting from 1 to 30 September 2014 at the Combat Training Education Depot (Dodiklatpur) Rindam V/Brawijaya and the Marine Combat Training Center (Puslatmar), Situbondo. This exercise also attended by [[Commanding General, United States Army Pacific|Commanding General, U.S. Army Pacific]] Gen. [[Vincent K. Brooks|Vincent K.Brooks]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Veasley |first=Matthew |date=24 September 2014 |title=Garuda Shield 2014: Army Pacific Commanding General, Gen. Vincent K. Brooks visit |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/image/1571024/garuda-shield-2014-army-pacific-commanding-general-gen-vincent-k-brooks-visit |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref>

Approximately 1,055 personnel consisting of 619 [[Kostrad]] soldiers under the leadership of Colonel Inf. [[Agung Pambudi]] (Danbrigif 6/2/K) as the Exercise Commander; and 436 soldiers from the [[United States Army Pacific|U.S. Army Pacific (USARPAC)]] under the leadership of Brigadier General [[Lewinz]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=5 September 2014 |title=Upacara Pembukaan Latma Garuda Shield-8 Tahun 2014 |url=https://tniad.mil.id/upacara-pembukaan-latma-garuda-shield-8-tahun-2014/ |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref>

Soldiers from the 2nd Brigade, 2nd Infantry Division based in Washington State, the 29th Infantry Brigade Combat Team, Hawaii Army National Guard, and the 25th Combat Aviation Brigade, [[25th Infantry Division (United States)|25th Infantry Division]] with Indonesian Army soldiers from the 2nd Kostrad Infantry Division carried out a month long exercise to foster cooperation and understanding.<ref name=":5">{{Cite news |first=Brian C. |last=Erickson |date=2 September 2014 |title=Indonesian, U.S. Exercise Garuda Shield Begins in East Java |url=http://www.pacom.mil:80/Media/News/Article/564551/indonesian-us-exercise-garuda-shield-begins-in-east-java/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161103010642/http://www.pacom.mil:80/Media/News/Article/564551/indonesian-us-exercise-garuda-shield-begins-in-east-java/ |archive-date=3 November 2016 |access-date=27 May 2025 |work=U.S. Pacific Command |language=en-US}}</ref>

Garuda Shield 2014 joint exercise consists of Command Training Operation Exercise, Command Post Exercise, Jungle Field Training Exercise, combat vehicle and aviation training, Combined Arms Fire Exercise, Medical, as well as social service activities.<ref name=":5"/>

===Garuda Shield 2015===
[[File:150821-A-ZD093-313 (20680842558).jpg|thumb|U.S. Army soldiers from Bravo Company 2-27th Infantry Regiment 3rd Infantry Brigade 25th Infantry Division, alongside Indonesian Army soldiers from 1st Infantry Division of Kostrad carry out Military Operations in Urban Terrain during Garuda Shield 2015 at Cibenda, West Java, Indonesia, on 21 August 2015.]]
Joint Exercise Garuda Shield 2015 between the Indonesian Army and the United States Army officially began and was opened in a military ceremony at the Kostrad Training Area, Gunung Sentul, [[Sukabumi Regency|Sukabumi]], 20 August 2015. Acting as the Inspector of the Ceremony was the Chief of Staff, 1st Infantry Division, Kostrad, Brigadier General [[Agus Suhardi]] and Deputy Commander of the 25th Infantry Division USARPAC Brig. General [[Gary Brito]]. The exercise also attended by Maj. General [[Edward F. Dorman III]], commander, [[8th Theater Sustainment Command]] for U.S. Army Pacific.<ref>{{Cite web |date=24 August 2015 |title=Latihan Bersama Garuda Shield-9 LIV TA. 2015 |url=https://tni.mil.id/view-82505-latihan-bersama-garuda-shield-9-liv-ta-2015.html |website=tni.mil.id |language=Indonesian}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |first=Brian |last=Erickson |date=20 August 2015 |title=Opening ceremony officially marks beginning of Garuda Shield 15 |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/news/173991/opening-ceremony-officially-marks-beginning-garuda-shield-15 |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref>

The Garuda Shield 2015 was carried out from 20 to 28 August 2015, involving 830 soldiers from both countries consisting of 380 Indonesian Army soldiers from the 328th Infantry Battalion (Yonif Linud-328/17/1), [[Kostrad 1st Infantry Division]] and 450 United States Army soldiers from the [[25th Infantry Division (United States)|25th Infantry Division]] for USARPAC. The exercise consist of Medical/Tactical Combat Casualty Care, Combat Patrol, marksmanship, Military Operations in Urban Terrain, Close Quarter Battle (CQB), Swamp Forest Patrol, and jungle and sea survival.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 August 2015 |title=Latihan Menembak Dalam Ajang Latma Garuda Shield 9 Tahun 2015 |url=https://tni.mil.id/view-82946-latihan-menembak-dalam-ajang-latma-garuda-shield-9-tahun-2015.html |website=tni.mil.id |language=Indonesian}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |first=Brian |last=Erickson |date=28 August 2015 |title=Wolfhounds and TNI Soldiers close out Garuda Shield 2015 |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/news/174735/wolfhounds-and-tni-soldiers-close-out-garuda-shield-2015 |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref>

===Garuda Shield 2016===
Joint Exercise Garuda Shield 2016 was held on 1 to 12 August 2016, attended by 481 joint military personnel from the Kostrad Raider Battalion and the U.S. Army Pacific at Asembagus Combat Training Center (''Puslatpur''), [[Situbondo Regency|Situbondo]], led by the Commander of 2nd Infantry Division Kostrad, Maj. Gen. [[Ganip Warsito]] and Commander of Hawaii Army National Guard Brigadier General [[Keith Tamashiro]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=3 August 2016 |title=Geladi Bersih Jelang Latma Garuda Shield |url=https://tni.mil.id/view-100111-geladi-bersih-jelang-latma-garuda-shield.html |website=tni.mil.id |language=Indonesian}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=14 August 2016 |title=Penutupan Latihan Bersama Garuda Shield ke-10 Tahun 2016 |url=https://tniad.mil.id/penutupan-latihan-bersama-garuda-shield-ke-10-tahun-2016/ |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref> 

The joint training materials between the two countries include, Command Post Exercise, Field Training Exercise including Counter Improvised Explosive Device (C-IED) training, Medical Exercise and Aviation Exercise.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=29 July 2016 |title=Prajurit Kostrad Tingkatkan Kesiapan Jelang Latma Garuda Shield-10 Tahun 2016 |url=https://tniad.mil.id/prajurit-kostrad-tingkatkan-kesiapan-jelang-latma-garuda-shield-10-tahun-2016/ |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=19 September 2016 |title=USARPAC Soldiers Assist Indonesian Soldiers With C-IED Training |url=https://www.army.mil/article/175302/usarpac_soldiers_assist_indonesian_soldiers_with_c_ied_training |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=www.army.mil |language=en}}</ref>

===Garuda Shield 2017===
[[File:Garuda Shield 2017 Closing Ceremony.jpg|thumb|Garuda Shield 2017 Closing Ceremony, 29 September 2017.]]

The Indonesian Army and the United States Army held the Garuda Shield 2017 in two different training locations, 310th Battalion Infantry Base (''Mayonif 310/KK")'' Cikembar, and Kostrad Cibenda Training Area, [[Sukabumi Regency|Sukabumi]], [[West Java]], for 11 days from 18 to 29 September 2017.<ref name=":6" /> The exercise led by Maj. Gen. [[Arthur J. Logan]], Hawaii Adjutant General and Brig. Gen. [[Joko Putranto]], Chief of Staff, [[Kostrad 1st Infantry Division]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=A. Foster |first=Matthew |date=29 September 2017 |title=Inspection |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/image/3832003/inspection |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref>

The exercise involved 732 personnel from the Indonesian Army from the 303rd Para Raider Infantry Battalion (Yonif 303/SSM), 13th Raider Infantry Brigade (Brigif 13/1) assigned to [[Kostrad 1st Infantry Division]] and Army Aviation (''Penerbad''), together with the US Army from the United States Army Pacific (USARPAC); and [[103rd Infantry Division (United States)|103rd Infantry Division]]; and [[United States Army Aviation Branch|US Army Aviation]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 September 2017 |title=TNI Angkatan Darat gelar latihan bersama tentara AS |url=https://www.antaranews.com/berita/653317/tni-angkatan-darat-gelar-latihan-bersama-tentara-as |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=Antara News |language=id}}</ref>

The Garuda Shield 2017 joint exercise consists of an early entry aviation Subject Matter Expert Exchange (SMEE) and unmanned aerial surveillance SMEE, aviation live fire exercises (surface and littoral), a Command Post Exercise, Combined Tactical Operation Center, and an infantry company Field Training Exercise and Live Fire Exercise (LFX).<ref>{{Cite web |date=18 September 2017 |title=STAND-TO! |url=https://www.army.mil/standto/archive/2017/09/18/ |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=www.army.mil |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=22 September 2017 |title=Latma Garuda Shield, Ajang Berbagi Ilmu Militer dan Pererat Kerja Sama TNI AD Dengan US Army |url=https://tniad.mil.id/latma-garuda-shield-ajang-berbagi-ilmu-militer-dan-pererat-kerja-sama-tni-ad-dengan-us-army/ |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=29 September 2017 |title=Pangdivif 1 Kostrad Tinjau Latma Garuda Shield-11/2017 di Sukabaumi |url=https://tniad.mil.id/pangdivif-1-kostrad-tinjau-latma-garuda-shield-112017-di-sukabaumi/ |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref> The exercise involved helicopters from both countries, with the Indonesian Army deploying Mi-35, Mi-17, Bell and Bolcow combat helicopters; and the US Army deploying Blackhawk and Apache helicopters.<ref name=":6">{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=1 October 2017 |title=Latma Garuda Shield-11 Resmi Ditutup |url=https://tniad.mil.id/latma-garuda-shield-11-resmi-ditutup/ |access-date=27 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref>

===Garuda Shield 2018===
Indiana Army National Guardsmen from the [[76th Infantry Brigade Combat Team (United States)|76th Infantry Brigade Combat Team]], with Indonesian Army soldiers from the 9th Raider Infantry Brigade, assigned to [[Kostrad 2nd Infantry Division]], held the Opening Ceremony of Garuda Shield 2018 at the Combat Training Center (''Puslatpur''), Situbondo, Indonesia, 29 July 2018.<ref name="AutoPD">{{Cite web |first=Marshall |last=Howell |date=1 August 2018 |title=Ceremony Marks Opening of Garuda Shield 2018 |url=https://www.war.gov/News/News-Stories/Article/Article/1590490/ceremony-marks-opening-of-garuda-shield-2018/ |website=def.gov}}{{source-attribution}}</ref>

Indonesian army Maj. Gen. [[Marga Taufiq]], the commander of the Kostrad 2nd Infantry Division, also welcomed the Hawaii National Guard Adjutant General, Army Maj. Gen. [[Arthur J. Logan]], as his co-host of the opening ceremony while emphasizing the shared respect between the partner armies.<ref name="AutoPD" />

The Garuda Shield 2018 joint exercise was held for 2 weeks, from 30 July 2018 until 10 August 2018, which included Command Training Operation Exercise, Command Post Exercise, Field Training Exercise, Aviation and Medical as well as Community Service activities.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=5 August 2018 |title=Garuda Shield-12/2018, Brigif Raider 9 Kostrad Berlatih dengan US Army. |url=https://tniad.mil.id/garuda-shield-122018-brigif-raider-9-kostrad-berlatih-dengan-us-army/ |access-date=28 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=1 August 2018 |title=Pangdiv 2 Kostrad Buka Latma Garuda Shield 2018 |url=https://beritalima.com/pangdiv-2-kostrad-buka-latma-garuda-shield-2018/ |access-date=28 May 2025 |website=Beritalima.com |language=id-ID}}</ref>

===Garuda Shield 2019===
[[File:Garuda Shield 2019 - Opening Ceremony (Photo ID 5681183).jpg|thumb|The 2019 Garuda Shield leaders from both armies pose for a picture with a formation of U.S. and Indonesian forces during the 2019 Garuda Shield opening ceremony 19 August 2019, at Dodiklatpur, Indonesia.]]
Indonesian Army soldiers from the 9th Raider Infantry Brigade, assigned to [[Kostrad 2nd Infantry Division]], and the US Army from United States Army Pacific (USARPAC) held the Opening Ceremony of Garuda Shield 2019, led by Commander of Kostrad 2nd Infantry Division Maj. Gen. [[Tri Yuniarto]] and Deputy Commanding General for the United States Army Pacific Maj. Gen. [[John P. Johnson (general)|Pete Johnson]] at Combat Training and Education Center (''Dodiklatpur'') Kodam V/Brw, Asembagus, [[Situbondo Regency|Situbondo]], Indonesia, 19 August 2019. The joint training was held for 12 days from 19 to 30 August 2019.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Leah |last=Ganoni |date=20 August 2019 |title=Celebrating 70 years of partnership at the Garuda Shield 2019 Opening Ceremony |url=https://www.pacom.mil/Media/NEWS/News-Article-View/Article/1939388/celebrating-70-years-of-partnership-at-the-garuda-shield-2019-opening-ceremony/ |work=pacom.mil}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=20 August 2019 |title=Latihan Bersama Garuda Shield-13 2019 Secara Resmi Dibuka Oleh Pangdivif 2 Kostrad |url=https://tni.mil.id/view-157736-latihan-bersama-garuda-shield13-2019-secara-resmi-dibuka-oleh-pangdivif-2-kostrad.html |website=tni.mil.id}}</ref>

More than 700 U.S. Army personnel from 1st Battalion, 27th Infantry Regiment, 2nd Infantry Brigade Combat Team assigned to [[25th Infantry Division (United States)|25th Infantry Division]]; Hawaii, U.S. Army Pacific Command; Hawaii, [[10th Regional Support Group|10th Support Group]], Japan, I Corps, Washington, and [[Army National Guard|U.S. Army National Guard]] from Michigan participated in Exercise Garuda Shield 19, making it not only one of the largest bilateral training exercises in the Indo-Pacific region but a true total force representation of the U.S. Army.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Leah |last=Ganoni |date=30 August 2019 |title=70-Year Partnership Achieves New Heights at Exercise Garuda Shield 19 |url=https://www.pacom.mil/Media/News/News-Article-View/Article/1949237/70-year-partnership-achieves-new-heights-at-exercise-garuda-shield-19/ |work=pacom.mil}}</ref>

===Garuda Shield 2020===
Garuda Shield 2020 (GS-14/2020) was opened in 9 September 2020. This exercise focuses on MDMP (Military Decision-Making Process) exercises, through conference (Indoor / computer simulation class). This exercise is limited due to [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref name=":13" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=adrian |first=beny |date=9 September 2020 |title=Latma Garuda Shield-14/2020 Akan Fokus Pada Latihan Military Decision Making Process |url=https://mylesat.com/2020/09/09/latma-garuda-shield-14-2020-akan-fokus-pada-latihan-military-decision-making-process/ |access-date= |website=Mylesat |language=Indonesian}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Komando |first=Portal |date=15 September 2020 |title=Pangdivif 1 Kostrad Tinjau Kegiatan Latma Garuda Shield-14/2020 |url=https://www.portal-komando.com/2020/09/pangdivif-1-kostrad-tinjau-kegiatan-latma-garuda-shield-14-2020/ |access-date= |language=id}}</ref>

===Garuda Shield 2021===
[[File:Garuda Shield 2021 opening ceremony.jpg|thumb|Garuda Shield 2021 opening ceremony at Baturaja, South Sumatra, 6 August 2021.]]

The Opening Ceremony of Garuda Shield 2021 was held on 4 August 2021, and was attended by the Commanding General of the United States Army Pacific (USARPAC), General [[Charles A. Flynn]], and the Chief of Staff of the Indonesian Army, General [[Andika Perkasa]] at the Army ''Kodiklat'' (Combat Training Center), Baturaja, Ogan Komering Ulu, South Sumatra.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hermawan |first=Nandang |date=17 August 2021 |title=Upacara Pembukaan Garuda Shield ke-15 Tahun 2021 di Baturaja, Sumatera Selatan |url=https://tniad.mil.id/upacara-pembukaan-garuda-shield-ke-15-tahun-2021-baturaja/ |access-date=28 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref>

The Garuda Shield 2021 joint exercise took place from 4 to 14 August 2021, with 2,161 Indonesian Army soldiers and 1,547 United States soldiers participating. A number of materials were implemented in this exercise, including: Staff Exercise, Field Training Exercise, Live Fire Exercise, Aviation and Medical Exercise (Medex) and two training programs that will be combined, namely Joint Combined Exchange Training and Garuda Airborne.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=5 August 2021 |title=Garuda Shield 2021: Latihan Tempur TNI AD-Militer AS Terbesar |url=https://www.cnnindonesia.com/nasional/20210805070517-20-676595/garuda-shield-2021-latihan-tempur-tni-ad-militer-as-terbesar/amp |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210805012126/https://www.cnnindonesia.com/nasional/20210805070517-20-676595/garuda-shield-2021-latihan-tempur-tni-ad-militer-as-terbesar/amp |archive-date=5 August 2021 |access-date=28 May 2025 |website=cnnindonesia.com |language=id-ID}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |first=Rachel |last=Williams |date=20 August 2021 |title=62nd AW Supports Garuda Shield 21, Strengthens Joint Interoperability |url=https://www.pacom.mil/Media/News/News-Article-View/Article/2741067/62nd-aw-supports-garuda-shield-21-strengthens-joint-interoperability/ |work=pacom.mil}}</ref>

== Super Garuda Shield 2022==
[[File:Indonesian Soldiers conduct live hoist training during Exercise Super Garuda Shield 22 at Baturaja.jpg|thumb|Indonesian Soldiers conduct live hoist training during Exercise Super Garuda Shield 2022 at Baturaja, Indonesia on 1 August 2022.]]
[[File:Super Garuda Shield 2022 Showcases Multinational Partnership and Joint Interoperability (Photo ID 7353975, VIRIN 220803-A-TP734-0006).jpg|thumb|Gen. [[Andika Perkasa]], Commander in Chief of the Indonesian National Armed Forces and Gen. [[Charles A. Flynn|Charles Flynn]], Commanding General of the U.S. Army Pacific salutes the formation of troops during the opening ceremony of Super Garuda Shield 2022, Baturaja, Indonesia, 3 August 2022.]]
[[File:Angkatan Pertahanan Australia mengikuti Latihan Garuda Shield untuk pertama kali.jpg|thumb|Soldiers from Australian Defense Force joined the Super Garuda Shield multinational exercise for the first time, 5 August 2022.]]
In April 2022, a new Garuda Shield joint-exercise was announced, which involved 14 countries, making it the largest edition of Garuda Shield by participants since it was established.<ref>{{cite news|title=Soldiers from 14 nations to take part in Indonesian-US war games|url=https://www.thejakartapost.com/world/2022/04/10/soldiers-from-14-nations-to-take-part-in-indonesian-us-war-games-.html|accessdate=18 April 2022|newspaper=The Jakarta Post|date=11 April 2022|agency=}}</ref>

The Opening Ceremony of '''Super Garuda Shield''' 2022 held on 3 August 2022, attended by the [[Commanding General, United States Army Pacific|Commanding General of the U.S. Army Pacific]], General [[Charles A. Flynn|Charles Flynn]], and the [[Commander of the Indonesian National Armed Forces]], General [[Andika Perkasa]], at [[Baturaja]] Combat Training Center (''Puslatpur''), South Sumatra, Indonesia.<ref name=":7" />

The exercise was conducted from 3 to 14 August 2022 by more than 4,000 combined forces personnel, including first time participants Australia, Singapore, and Japan Ground Self Defense Force, are participating in support of the exercise.<ref name=":8">{{Cite web |title=Garuda Shield expanded - Wed, August 3, 2022 |url=https://www.thejakartapost.com/paper/2022/08/02/garuda-shield-expanded.html |access-date=28 May 2025 |website=The Jakarta Post |language=en}}</ref> Other nations include Canada, France, India, Malaysia, New Zealand, the Republic of Korea, Papua New Guinea, Timor Leste, and the United Kingdom as Observer.<ref name=":7">{{cite web|title=Super Garuda Shield 2022 Showcases Multinational Partnership and Joint Interoperability |url=https://id.usembassy.gov/super-garuda-shield-2022-showcases-multinational-partnership-and-joint-interoperability/|website=US Embassy in Indonesia|date=3 August 2022|access-date=6 October 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Sumatra party signals low-key end to Super Garuda Shield exercise in Indonesia |url=https://www.stripes.com/theaters/asia_pacific/2022-08-15/garuda-shield-indonesia-military-exercise-6988985.html|website=stripes.com|date=15 August 2022|access-date=6 October 2022}}</ref><ref name=":9">{{Cite web |last=Ria Rizki Nirmala Sari |date=3 August 2022 |title=Super Garuda Shield 2022 Dimulai, 4.337 Personel Dari 13 Negara Latihan Bersama di Indonesia |url=https://www.suara.com/news/2022/08/03/144839/super-garuda-shield-2022-dimulai-4337-personel-dari-13-negara-latihan-bersama-di-indonesia |access-date=28 May 2025 |website=suara.com |language=id}}</ref>

The exercise consisted Field Training Exercise, Medic Exercise, Combined Arms Life Fire Exercise, Counter-Improvised Explosive Devices, Ordnance Disposal, Aviation, and Subject Matter Expert Exchange. As well as Joint Exercises: Amphibious Exercise, Cooperative Deployment, Himars Rapid Infiltration/ Caesar Rapid Infiltration, Austere Airfield Ops and Airborne Operations.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kodam VI/Mulawarman |date=5 August 2022 |title=Latma Super Garuda Shield Tahun 2022 Resmi Di Buka |url=https://ppid.tniad.mil.id/index.php/i/3599/latma%20-super%20-garuda%20-shield%20-tahun%20-2022%20-resmi%20-di%20-buka |access-date=28 May 2025 |website=ppid.tniad.mil.id}}</ref>

