== Super Garuda Shield 2023 ==
[[File:Group of Australian soldiers aiming EF88 rifles during Exercise Super Garuda Shield 2023.jpg|thumb|A group of Australian Defense Force Soldiers, engages the opposing force with their assigned weapons during a Field Training Exercise during Exercise Super Garuda Shield 2023, 6 September 2023.]]
[[File:Super Garuda Shield 2023 – Multi-Lateral Amphibious Assault (Photo ID 8014425).jpg|thumb|Soldiers from U.S. Marine Corps, Japan Ground Self-Defense Force, and Indonesian Marine Corps during amphibious assault in Super Garuda Shield 2023, 10 September 2023.]]
[[File:Super Garuda Shield 2023 - Singaporean Armed Forces (SAF) carry out Amphibious Landing.jpg|thumb|Singapore Armed Forces (SAF) soldiers carried out an amphibious landing using LVT-7 during the Super Garuda Shield (SGS) 2023 Joint Exercise at Banongan Beach, 5th Marine Combat Training Center (Puslatpurmar) Baluran, Situbondo, East Java, Sunday, 10 September 2023.]]
On 31 August 2023, Super Garuda Shield 2023 launched at Warships Training Center (''Puslatkaprang''), 2nd Fleet Command (''Koarmada II''), [[Surabaya|Surabaya, East Java]] led by Commodore [[Edi Haryanto]], Commander of the Naval Battle Group, 2nd Fleet Command and U.S. Maj. General [[Jered Helwig|Jered P. Helwig]], Commanding General, [[8th Theater Sustainment Command]]; and at 5th Combat Training Center (''Puslatpur 5''), [[Baluran National Park|Baluran]], [[Situbondo Regency|Situbondo]], East Java, attended by Admiral [[Yudo Margono]], Commander of the Indonesian National Armed Forces and Lt. Gen. [[Xavier Brunson]], [[List of commanders of I Corps (United States)|Commanding General of the U.S. Army’s I Corps]]. Staff exercises between the US, Indonesia, the UK, and Australia were also held in addition to the regular exercises.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=1 September 2023 |title=Senior U.S. and Indonesian Military Leaders Launch Super Garuda Shield 2023 |url=https://id.usembassy.gov/senior-u-s-and-indonesian-military-leaders-launch-super-garuda-shield-2023/ |access-date=6 March 2024 |website=U.S. Embassy & Consulates in Indonesia |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2 September 2023 |title=Pangkostrad Hadiri Pembukaan Latihan Super Garuda Shield 2023 |url=https://tniad.mil.id/pangkostrad-hadiri-pembukaan-latihan-super-garuda-shield-2023/ |access-date=29 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref>

The exercise was conducted from 31 August to 13 September 2023 by more than 5,000 combined forces personnel from seven nations participating in support of the exercise, and other twelve nations as the Observers.<ref name=":10">{{Cite web |date=14 September 2023 |title=ADF successfully completes interoperability training in Indonesia |url=https://www.defence.gov.au/news-events/releases/2023-09-14/adf-successfully-completes-interoperability-training-indonesia |website=defence.gov.au}}</ref><ref name=":11">{{Cite web |date=28 August 2023 |title=United States, Indonesia, and Five Other Nations to Begin Super Garuda Shield 2023 |url=https://id.usembassy.gov/united-states-indonesia-and-five-other-nations-to-begin-super-garuda-shield-2023/ |access-date=29 May 2025 |website=U.S. Embassy & Consulates in Indonesia |language=en-US}}</ref>

The exercise consisted Subject Matter Expert Exchange (SMEE) and engineering project (ENCAP); Joint Staff Exercise; Joint Field Training Exercise (FTX): Jungle FTX, Military Operations in Urban Terrain (MOUT), Maritime Operation, Airborne Assault, Special Operation; Austere Airfield; HIRAIN/C-RAIN; Amphibious Assault; and Combined Arms Live Fire Exercise (CALFEX).<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 September 2023 |title=Operational Staff Exercise Super Garuda Shield Opening Ceremony |url=https://www.pacom.mil/Media/News/News-Article-View/Article/3514301/operational-staff-exercise-super-garuda-shield-opening-ceremony/ |website=pacom.mil}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Joseph Clark |date=12 September 2023 |title=Super Garuda Shield: U.S., Partners Train in Indo-Pacific |url=https://www.war.gov/News/News-Stories/Article/Article/3523152/super-garuda-shield-us-partners-train-in-indo-pacific/ |website=United States Department of Defense |language=En}}</ref>

