== Super Garuda Shield 2024 ==
[[File:Super Garuda Shield 2024 - Opening Ceremony (Photo ID 8609771).jpg|thumb|Multinational service members pose for a group photo following the opening ceremony of Super Garuda Shield 2024 at Juanda International Airport, East Java, Indonesia, 26 August 2024.]]
[[File:Amphibious Assault - Super Garuda Shield 2024.jpg|thumb|U.S. Marine and Indonesian Marine participate in an Amphibious Assault exercise as part of Super Garuda Shield 2024 near Banongan, Indonesia, 5 September 2024.]]
[[File:Super Garuda Shield 2024 - Amphibious Operation - Infiltration.jpg|thumb|Soldiers from U.S. Marine Corps, Indonesian Marine Corps and Amphibious Rapid Deployment Brigade Reconnaissance Company of Japan Ground Self-Defense Force (JGSDF) carried out amphibious assault during Super Garuda Shield 2024.]]

United States and the Indonesian National Armed Forces officially kicked off the 2024 Super Garuda Shield exercise on 26 August 2024 with an opening ceremony at Indonesian military base on Juanda Naval Air Base, [[Surabaya]], [[East Java]], Indonesia.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |date=27 August 2024 |title=United States and Indonesia Kick Off Multinational Super Garuda Shield 2024 |url=https://id.usembassy.gov/united-states-and-indonesia-kick-off-multinational-super-garuda-shield-2024/ |access-date= |website=U.S. Embassy & Consulates in Indonesia |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=27 August 2024 |title=United States and Indonesia Kick Off Multinational Super Garuda Shield 2024 |url=https://www.usarpac.army.mil/Our-Story/Our-News/Article-Display/Article/3886404/united-states-and-indonesia-kick-off-multinational-super-garuda-shield-2024/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250307153356/https://www.usarpac.army.mil/Our-Story/Our-News/Article-Display/Article/3886404/united-states-and-indonesia-kick-off-multinational-super-garuda-shield-2024/ |archive-date=7 March 2025 |access-date= |work=U.S. Army Pacific |language=en-US}}</ref>

The exercise attended by the Commander of the [[United States Indo-Pacific Command|U.S. Indo-Pacific Command]] Admiral [[Samuel Paparo|Samuel J. Paparo]], Commander of the Indonesian National Armed Forces General [[Agus Subiyanto]], and U.S. Ambassador to Indonesia [[Kamala Shirin Lakhdhir|Kamala S. Lakhdhir]], including other senior government and military leaders.<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 September 2024 |title=U.S. Indo-Pacific Commander Travels to Indonesia |url=https://www.pacom.mil/Media/NEWS/Article/3891919/us-indo-pacific-commander-travels-to-indonesia/ |website=pacom.mil}}</ref>

Super Garuda Shield 2024 (SGS24) multinational exercise was held by partnering nations on 26 August 2024 – 6 September 2024, in three main locations: [[Situbondo Regency|Situbondo]], [[Karawang]], and [[Baturaja]].<ref>{{Cite news |date=6 September 2024 |title=Super Garuda Shield 2024: Uniting Forces at the Joint Operations Center |url=https://www.pacom.mil/Media/News/News-Article-View/Article/3898325/super-garuda-shield-2024-uniting-forces-at-the-joint-operations-center/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250321175858/https://www.pacom.mil/Media/NEWS/News-Article-View/Article/3898325/super-garuda-shield-2024-uniting-forces-at-the-joint-operations-center/ |archive-date=21 March 2025 |access-date= |work=U.S. Indo-Pacific Command |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":2">{{Cite web |date=22 August 2024 |title=United States, Indonesia, and Eight Partner Nations to Begin Super Garuda Shield 2024 |url=https://id.usembassy.gov/united-states-indonesia-and-eight-partner-nations-to-begin-super-garuda-shield-2024/#:~:text=Service%20members%20from%20the%20United,Arabia,%20Thailand,%20and%20Vanuatu. |access-date= |website=U.S. Embassy & Consulates in Indonesia |language=en-US}}</ref> Service members from the United States, Indonesia, Australia, Canada, France, Japan, Singapore, South Korea, United Kingdom, and New Zealand participated in the exercise, including Observing nations from Brazil, Brunei, Fiji, Germany, India, Malaysia, Netherlands, Papua New Guinea, Philippines, Saudi Arabia, Thailand, and Vanuatu. The total number of Participants from all countries is approximately 6,946 service members.<ref name=":2" /><ref name=":12">{{Cite web |last=Indonesiadefense |date=6 September 2024 |title=Super Garuda Shield sebagai Upaya TNI Adopsi Model Pertempuran Masa Depan |url=https://indonesiadefense.com/super-garuda-shield-sebagai-upaya-tni-adopsi-model-pertempuran-masa-depan/ |access-date= |website=Indonesiadefense.com |language=id}}</ref>

The exercise involves various military activities: Joint Staff Exercise (STAFFEX), Cyber Exercise (CYBEREX), Subject Matter Expert Exchanges (SMEE), Airborne Ops, Cargo Delivery System, Joint Strike, Jungle Field Training Exercise, Special Operation Force, Amphibious Operation, Engineering Civic Action Program (ENCAP), including Combined Arms Life Fire Exercise (CALFEX).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Gutierrez |first=Osmar |date=5 September 2024 |title=Super Garuda Shield 2024 {{!}} USS Green Bay participates in an Amphibious Exercise |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/image/8626472/super-garuda-shield-2024-uss-green-bay-participates-amphibious-exercise |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wilson |first=Evangelos |date=5 September 2024 |title=Marine Amphibious Assault |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/image/8624886/marine-amphibious-assault |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Aguilar |first=Mariah |date=6 September 2024 |title=Super Garuda Shield 2024: CALFEX (Live-Fire) |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/image/8627984/super-garuda-shield-2024-calfex-live-fire |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":12" /><ref>{{Cite web |title=Rape fortress Indo-Pacific through Super Garuda Shield 2024 |url=https://www.antarafoto.com/photo-story/view/2517/rape-fortress-indo-pacific-through-super-garuda-shield-2024#:~:text=Prajurit%20marinir%20indonesia%20and%20SAF,5%20Replies,%20Karangtekok,%20Situbondo. |access-date=24 May 2025 |website=antarafoto.com |language=en}}</ref> The peak exercise, which involved a ground attack, was carried out at the 5th Marine Combat Training Center (''Puslatpurmar 5''), [[Baluran]], Situbondo, East Java, Indonesia.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Melanie |last=Tolen |date=4 September 2024 |title=Super Garuda Shield 2024: 'Joint strike' exercise demos an F-16, live fire in East Java |url=https://www.pacom.mil/Media/News/News-Article-View/Article/3893548/super-garuda-shield-2024-joint-strike-exercise-demos-an-f-16-live-fire-in-east/ |access-date= |work=Pacom.mil |pages=}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=MRF-D 24.3 U.S. Marines, Sailors strengthen partnerships during Super Garuda Shield 2024 |url=https://www.pacom.mil/Media/NEWS/News-Article-View/Article/3904529/mrf-d-243-us-marines-sailors-strengthen-partnerships-during-super-garuda-shield/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250417234747/https://www.pacom.mil/Media/News/News-Article-View/Article/3904529/mrf-d-243-us-marines-sailors-strengthen-partnerships-during-super-garuda-shield/ |archive-date=17 April 2025 |access-date= |work=U.S. Indo-Pacific Command |language=en-US}}</ref>

In addition, the exercise also included parachuting, airborne ops, and various other training materials, including at the Drop Zone (DZ) at Baturaja Combat Training Center (''Puslatpur Baturaja''), [[Ogan Komering Ulu Regency|Ogan Komering Ulu]], [[South Sumatra]], Indonesia.<ref>{{Cite web |date=31 August 2024 |title=Penerjun Tri Dharma Hiasi Langit Baturaja, Sukseskan Airborne Operation Super Garuda Shield 2024 |url=https://tniad.mil.id/penerjun-tri-dharma-hiasi-langit-baturaja-sukseskan-airborne-operation-super-garuda-shield-2024/ |access-date=25 May 2025 |website=tniad.mil.id |language=id}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=29 August 2024 |title=Super Garuda Shield 2024: Airborne Jump |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/image/8619817/super-garuda-shield-2024-airborne-jump |access-date=25 May 2025 |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=29 August 2024 |title=Super Garuda Shield 2024 Airborne Operation |url=https://www.dvidshub.net/image/8619911/super-garuda-shield-2024-airborne-operation |access-date= |website=DVIDS |language=en}}</ref>

